      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 73,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b9",
      "text": "LDPOM = LDPO + LMargin.\n(4)\n",
      "bbox": [
        120.66,
        182.7,
        290.11,
        195.28
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        482,
        730,
        1160,
        781
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "CMSY10",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 27,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b10",
      "text": "For simplicity, we refer to this combined objective LDPOM\nas DPO throughout the rest of the paper unless specified.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.44,
        199.98,
        288.44,
        222.26
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        221,
        799,
        1153,
        889
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.06,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 115,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b11",
      "text": "3.2. Decompose The Training Process\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.44,
        237.33,
        213.92,
        247.3
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        221,
        949,
        855,
        989
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 35,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b12",
      "text": "In this section, we decompose the training process to quan-\ntitatively analyze the emergence of language bias. Our\nanalysis begins with the VIT stage. We hypothesize that\nstandard conditional probability-based training may lead the\nmodel to neglect visual tokens due to the inherent modality\ngap. To test this, we track two key quantities during LLaVA\nv1.5 7B\u2019s instruction tuning:\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.19,
        256.08,
        291.1,
        337.77
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        220,
        1024,
        1164,
        1351
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 381,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b13",
      "text": "RVIT = log \u03c0\u03b8(y | x, v)\n",
      "bbox": [
        63.03,
        343.4,
        161.26,
        361.72
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        252,
        1373,
        645,
        1446
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "CMSY10",
      "is_math": true,
      "char_count": 23,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b14",
      "text": "\u03c0ref(y | x, v),\nBVIT = log \u03c0\u03b8(y | x)\n",
      "bbox": [
        112.59,
        343.4,
        265.41,
        368.07
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        450,
        1373,
        1061,
        1472
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 6.97,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": true,
      "char_count": 36,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b15",
      "text": "\u03c0ref(y | x), (5)\n",
      "bbox": [
        226.37,
        350.27,
        290.11,
        368.07
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        905,
        1401,
        1160,
        1472
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "CMMI10",
      "is_math": true,
      "char_count": 16,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b16",
      "text": "where \u03c0ref is the pre-VIT reference model. RVIT (reward)\nmeasures the gain on the full multimodal input, while BVIT\n(bias) measures the gain from text-only conditioning. As\nshown in Figure 3(a), their nearly identical trajectories are\nstrong quantitative evidence that the model\u2019s improvement\nis text-driven, substantiating the presence of language bias.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.08,
        372.59,
        290.36,
        442.69
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        220,
        1490,
        1161,
        1770
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.06,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": true,
      "char_count": 354,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b17",
      "text": "Similarly, we extend this analysis to DPO. We track the\ncorresponding multimodal gain (R) and text-only gain (B)\nfor both the preferred (yw) and rejected (yl) responses in\neach preference pair. Our experiments on the RLHF-V\ndataset reveal a consistent trend (Figure 3(b)). Notably,\nthe text-only gain for preferred responses (BDPOw) even\noutpaces the multimodal gain (RDPOw), reinforcing that\npreference learning can also exacerbate language bias at\nthe expense of visual grounding. Additional analysis and\nvisualizations of language bias dynamics during training are\nprovided in Appendix D.1.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.19,
        450.58,
        290.69,
        580.17
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        220,
        1802,
        1162,
        2320
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.06,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 593,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b18",
      "text": "Motivated by these findings, we formally define language\nbias as:\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.44,
        587.9,
        289.44,
        610.06
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        221,
        2351,
        1157,
        2440
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.05,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 65,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b19",
      "text": "B = log \u03c0\u03b8(y | x)\n",
      "bbox": [
        132.08,
        608.35,
        206.97,
        625.18
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        528,
        2433,
        827,
        2500
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "CMSY10",
      "is_math": true,
      "char_count": 17,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b20",
      "text": "\u03c0ref(y | x).\n(6)\n",
      "bbox": [
        167.93,
        615.22,
        290.11,
        633.02
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        671,
        2460,
        1160,
        2532
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 6.97,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": true,
      "char_count": 16,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b21",
      "text": "Intuitively, B quantifies the model\u2019s performance gain from\ntext-only conditioning relative to a reference model. A high\nB value indicates a strong reliance on its internal language\npriors, diminishing the contribution of the visual modal-\nity. This bias is a common artifact of multimodal training\nparadigms that rely on conditional probabilities, such as\nVIT and DPO.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.08,
        635.41,
        291.09,
        717.47
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        220,
        2541,
        1164,
        2869
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.9,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 369,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b22",
      "text": "4. Simple and Effective Mitigation of\nLanguage Bias\n",
      "bbox": [
        307.44,
        67.85,
        494.49,
        93.75
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1229,
        271,
        1977,
        375
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 51,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b23",
      "text": "Building on our quantitative formulation of language bias\nfrom Section 3, we introduce two simple yet highly effective\nmitigation strategies.\n",
      "bbox": [
        307.44,
        102.71,
        541.44,
        136.66
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1229,
        410,
        2165,
        546
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.06,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 141,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b24",
      "text": "4.1. Language Bias Regularization for Visual\nInstruction Tuning\n",
      "bbox": [
        307.44,
        151.74,
        497.51,
        173.66
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1229,
        606,
        1990,
        694
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 63,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b25",
      "text": "As established in our analysis, language bias is minimal\nafter the pre-training stage. Therefore, the primary goal\nduring Visual Instruction Tuning (VIT) is not to introduce\ncomplex new constraints, but simply to mitigate the ex-\ncessive growth of language bias. This prevents the model\nfrom over-relying on the linguistic modality at the expense\nof visual grounding.\n",
      "bbox": [
        307.08,
        182.36,
        543.09,
        264.13
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1228,
        729,
        2172,
        1056
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.06,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 367,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b26",
      "text": "To this end, we propose Language Bias Regularization\n(LBR), which directly penalizes the magnitude of the lan-\nguage bias term B:\n",
      "bbox": [
        307.11,
        271.94,
        543.09,
        305.98
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1228,
        1087,
        2172,
        1223
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.06,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 129,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b27",
      "text": "LLBR =\n",
      "bbox": [
        359.5,
        321.38,
        390.95,
        332.96
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
