      "is_math": true,
      "char_count": 26,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p4_b36",
      "text": "where \u03b1 is a hyperparameter controlling the regularization\nstrength. By minimizing LLBR, we constrain the model\u2019s\ntext-only output distribution (\u03c0\u03b8(y | x)) to remain close\nto that of the reference model. This simple mechanism\neffectively suppresses linguistic drift during training and\nencourages the model to better utilize visual information.\n",
      "bbox": [
        307.08,
        399.0,
        541.44,
        468.95
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1228,
        1596,
        2165,
